    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0255" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/202</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-05T18:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 8, 7.30
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1706. … Internal situation again threatening. Extreme socialists more aggressive
                    demanding removal of generals, claiming threatened counter [-revolution?]
                    justifies same. Had interview with Kerensky yesterday, endeavored to impress upon him necessity for
                    restoring discipline; to-day he promulgates proclamation appealing for support
                    of officers which first word utterances by him in that line.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
